; Test: Cross-matching two ACT queries
; =====================================
;
; Prerequisites: Create ACT file first
;   ./examples/misc/make_fruit_colors_act.sh
;
; Pattern: (I (ACT file1 <pat1>) (ACT file2 <pat2>))
; Queries TWO ACT files (or same file twice) with consistent bindings

; Test: Find items that appear in BOTH patterns in the ACT file
; The fruit_colors.act has facts like:
;   (color apple red)
;   (color banana yellow)

; This won't work perfectly because we only have one type of fact,
; but let's try finding the same fruit mentioned twice
(exec 0
  (I (ACT fruit_colors (color $fruit $c1))
     (ACT fruit_colors (color $fruit $c2)))
  (O (+ (fruit-has-colors $fruit $c1 $c2))))

; Expected: Each fruit paired with itself and others
; (fruit-has-colors apple red red)
; (fruit-has-colors banana yellow yellow)
; etc.
;
; Key insight: Multiple ACT queries can cross-match on shared variables!
